The numbers is a list of 1, 2, 3, and 1.
The last is the last position of numbers.
The peak is 0.
For every spot from 0 to last.
The higherleft is 1.
The higherright is 1.
If spot is more than 0 and item (spot minus 1) of numbers is at least item spot of numbers, set higherleft to 0.
If spot is less than last and item (spot plus 1) of numbers is at least item spot of numbers, set higherright to 0.
If higherleft is 1 and higherright is 1, set peak to spot.

Show peak.
